  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Using the reduction formulas, find expressions for each of the following in terms of multiple angles.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q19-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^{4}\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{8}(3+4\\cos 2\\theta+\\cos 4\\theta)$",
          "worked": "Apply the cosine reduction formula twice.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^{4}\\theta&=(\\cos^{2}\\theta)^{2}\\\\\\cos^{4}\\theta&=\\left(\\frac{1+\\cos 2\\theta}{2}\\right)^{2}\\\\\\cos^{4}\\theta&=\\frac{1}{4}(1+2\\cos 2\\theta+\\cos^{2}2\\theta)\\\\\\cos^{4}\\theta&=\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos 2\\theta+\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\frac{1+\\cos 4\\theta}{2}\\right)\\\\\\cos^{4}\\theta&=\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos 2\\theta+\\frac{1}{8}\\cos 4\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q19-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^{3}\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{4}(3\\sin\\theta-\\sin 3\\theta)$\n\nExpand $\\sin(2\\theta+\\theta)$ and rearrange.",
          "worked": "Use the compound-angle formula, then the double-angle and Pythagorean identities.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin 3\\theta&=\\sin(2\\theta+\\theta)\\\\\\sin 3\\theta&=\\sin 2\\theta\\cos\\theta+\\cos 2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\\sin 3\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos^{2}\\theta+(1-2\\sin^{2}\\theta)\\sin\\theta\\\\\\sin 3\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta(1-\\sin^{2}\\theta)+\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^{3}\\theta\\\\\\sin 3\\theta&=3\\sin\\theta-4\\sin^{3}\\theta\\\\\\sin^{3}\\theta&=\\frac{1}{4}(3\\sin\\theta-\\sin 3\\theta).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 75
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q19-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^{3}\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{4}(3\\cos\\theta+\\cos 3\\theta)$\n\nExpand $\\cos(2\\theta+\\theta)$ and rearrange.",
          "worked": "Use the compound-angle formula, then the double-angle and Pythagorean identities.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos(2\\theta+\\theta)\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos 2\\theta\\cos\\theta-\\sin 2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=(1-2\\sin^{2}\\theta)\\cos\\theta-2\\sin^{2}\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos\\theta-4\\cos\\theta\\sin^{2}\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos\\theta-4\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos^{2}\\theta)\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=4\\cos^{3}\\theta-3\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos^{3}\\theta&=\\frac{1}{4}(3\\cos\\theta+\\cos 3\\theta).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 75
      }
    ]
  },
